TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan; Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan; Image 1"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Information sources"},{"id":"R6","met":"yes","where":"Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The 10 m ground-sample-distance requirement is not yet demonstrated to detect bleaching reliably. Sensor spectral bands, water-column effects, turbidity, and validation against the cited mapping method need consideration."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"Weekly full-reef coverage and delivery within 24 hours are not yet established. The approximate ground-track spacing and swath discussion identifies a trade, but coverage needs orbit-access simulations that account for latitude, revisit, daylight, and cloud availability; data volume and downlink capacity also need assessment."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"The 97.8° sun-synchronous inclination is plausible at 600 km, but the report gives the target nodal precession without showing the J2 calculation or assumptions used to obtain that inclination."}],"overall":"A strong, coherent preliminary report that meets all six task requirements. The mission rationale, project plan, and early orbital work are particularly effective. The principal next step is to substantiate imaging and revisit feasibility, including sensor performance, cloud constraints, and communications capacity.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":9.0,"scale":10.0,"points":36.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"The mission purpose, Australian benefit, intended operational and research users, and preliminary measurable objectives are clear and well connected to user needs. The rationale is supported by references. Some claims and the proposed 10 m imaging requirement would benefit from stronger qualification or validation.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Give reef managers direct, repeatable observations of coral colour over the whole Great Barrier Reef"},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"The satellite would be operated by the Australian Institute of Marine Science (AIMS)."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Deliver each image to an Australian ground station within 24 hours of capture."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":9.0,"scale":10.0,"points":27.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"The Gantt chart and task descriptions give a feasible, mission-linked sequence, with deadlines, contingency actions, and appropriate planned information sources. The plan includes useful responses to schedule and software-access risks. A little more detail on task completion criteria would strengthen it further.","evidence":[{"where":"Image 1","quote":""},{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"The order follows the mission: the imaging requirements (objectives 1 and 2) fix the orbit altitude and local time"},{"where":"Contingencies","quote":"Week 10 is float as well as editing time: no new design work is planned in it."},{"where":"Information sources","quote":"Table 2 lists the sources I plan to use and what each is for."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Useful preliminary orbit calculations, an initial STK scenario, and an interpretation of the swath-versus-coverage challenge demonstrate progress. The period, approximate sun-synchronous inclination, and ground-track shift are reasonable. The inclination calculation is not shown, and the coverage conclusion remains a preliminary estimate rather than a simulated result.","evidence":[{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"I have also made first hand calculations for a candidate orbit, a circular sun-synchronous orbit at 600 km altitude"},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"T = 2π√(a³/μ) | 5,801 s = 96.7 min"},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"A first STK scenario with this orbit has been set up, and its period agrees with the hand calculation."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":16.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"The report has a logical structure, readable prose, clearly labelled tables and figure, and a matching reference list. Presentation is generally consistent and professional. Some phrasing is awkward, and a few sources are described imprecisely, but these do not impede understanding.","evidence":[{"where":"Image 1","quote":""},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"Table 3: Preliminary hand calculations for the candidate orbit."},{"where":"References","quote":"[7] J. R. Wertz, D. F. Everett, and J. J. Puschell, Eds."}]}]}
